# Task 8: Final Solution Summary

## Problem

Educational institutions receive a high volume of student queries through multiple channels such as chat, email, and portals. Manually reviewing and responding to these messages is time-consuming, inconsistent, and prone to delays, leading to poor student experience.


## Proposed AI Solution

An NLP-based automated system that classifies student messages based on sentiment and intent. The system will preprocess incoming text, convert it into numerical representations, and use a trained model to categorize messages. Based on the classification, queries can be prioritized and routed to the appropriate department.


## Required Data

The system requires historical student interaction data, including text messages, communication channels, and labeled categories such as sentiment or query type. The data is primarily unstructured text and must be cleaned and preprocessed before use.


## Model Recommendation

A transformer-based model (such as BERT) is recommended due to its ability to understand context and handle complex language patterns. For simpler implementation, a TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline can be used as a starting point.


## Expected Business Impact

The solution will reduce response time, improve efficiency in handling student queries, and enhance overall student satisfaction. It will also allow institutions to scale support operations without significantly increasing human resources. This also enables data-driven decision-making by identifying recurring student issues and trends.


## Risks and Mitigation Plan

Potential risks include biased predictions, incorrect classifications, and privacy concerns. These can be mitigated by using diverse training data, implementing human review mechanisms, and ensuring strict data protection practices. Regular monitoring and model updates will further improve reliability.
